    "exitCallout": "Exit interview feedback",
    "exitMessage": "Positives\nStrong Company Culture — Employees appreciated Aditi's positive work environment, supportive colleagues, and organizational values, with one rating the culture 10/10.\nAdequate Work Resources — Both employees confirmed being 100% equipped with the necessary tools, resources, and support to perform effectively.\nSupportive Leadership & Mentorship — Appreciated Abhishek and Aalap for their guidance and mentorship, along with Ashfaq's professional approach.\nStrong Performance Feedback — Manager acknowledged professionalism, ownership, technical expertise, and consistent contributions.\n\nConcerns\nManagerial Behavior (Indira) — Employee reported frequent yelling, harsh communication, and a perceived lack of respect from the reporting manager.\nEmployee Grievance Handling — Employee felt that concerns escalated to PD were not adequately addressed or followed up.\nManagerial Accountability & Team Morale — Employee reported repeated concerns during pulse connects without visible corrective action and indicated similar dissatisfaction among colleagues.\nCompensation Dissatisfaction — Employee expressed dissatisfaction with comparatively low compensation and salary increments that did not meet expectations.\nLimited Client Exposure — Following the conclusion of the Verizon engagement, the employee sought opportunities to work with larger clients.\nRemote Work Flexibility — The prospective employer offered remote working flexibility, influencing the employee's decision despite Aditi's compensation counteroffer.\nPost-Resignation Managerial Behavior — Employee reported a change in Aalap's behavior following resignation, despite an otherwise positive working relationship.",
